An activity network has the durations shown, in days.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},>=stealth]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (2,0);\coordinate (Q) at (3.5,-1.7);\coordinate (R) at (6,-1.7);\coordinate (Z) at (7.5,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(P) node[midway,above] {$A,6$};
\draw[->] (P)--(Z) node[midway,above] {$C,7$};
\draw[->] (P)--(Q) node[midway,above right] {$B,5$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(R) node[midway,below] {$D,2$};
\draw[->] (R)--(Z) node[midway,below right] {$E,3$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,Z}{\fill (\v) circle (2pt);}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Find the minimum completion time and explain whether reducing $C$ by $2$ days would shorten the project.
(b) Starting from the original durations, reduce $A$ by $2$ days. Find the new completion time and critical path.
(c) Starting from the original durations, reduce $B$ by $3$ days and $E$ by $2$ days. Find the new completion time, critical path and time saved.
(d) Starting from the original durations, what is the greatest useful reduction in $B$?

A refurbishment has the following activity durations, in days.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},>=stealth]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (2,1.5);\coordinate (Q) at (2,-1.5);\coordinate (R) at (4,0);\coordinate (T) at (6,1.5);\coordinate (U) at (6,-1.5);\coordinate (Z) at (8,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$A,3$};
\draw[->] (S)--(Q) node[midway,below left] {$B,5$};
\draw[->] (P)--(R) node[pos=0.3,above right,xshift=2mm,yshift=2mm] {$C,8$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(R) node[pos=0.3,below right,xshift=2mm,yshift=-2mm] {$D,4$};
\draw[->] (R)--(T) node[pos=0.7,above left,xshift=-2mm,yshift=2mm] {$E,5$};
\draw[->] (R)--(U) node[pos=0.7,below left,xshift=-2mm,yshift=-2mm] {$F,4$};
\draw[->] (T)--(Z) node[midway,above right] {$G,3$};
\draw[->] (U)--(Z) node[midway,below right] {$H,5$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,T,U,Z}{\fill (\v) circle (2pt);}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) What is the greatest useful reduction in $C$ alone?
(b) Only $C$, $F$ and $H$ can be shortened. Their costs are $\$500$, $\$300$ and $\$450$ per day, respectively. Each can be reduced to zero. Shorten the project as much as possible for the least cost. State the reductions, final completion time and cost.

A renovation has the activity durations shown, in days.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont},>=stealth]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (2,1.5);\coordinate (Q) at (2,-1.5);\coordinate (R) at (4.7,1.5);\coordinate (T) at (4.7,-1.5);\coordinate (Z) at (7,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$A,10$};
\draw[->] (S)--(Q) node[midway,below left] {$B,4$};
\draw[->] (P)--(R) node[midway,above] {$C,7$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(R) node[midway,above left] {$D,6$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(T) node[midway,below] {$E,3$};
\draw[->] (R)--(Z) node[midway,above right] {$F,8$};
\draw[->] (T)--(Z) node[midway,below right] {$G,7$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,T,Z}{\fill (\v) circle (2pt);}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Only $A$ and $C$ can be shortened: $A$ by at most $5$ days at $\$120$ per day, and $C$ by at most $4$ days at $\$180$ per day. Find the least cost of shortening the project as much as possible.
(b) Instead, four activities can be shortened: $A$ by at most $3$ days at $\$120$ per day, $C$ by at most $2$ days at $\$180$ per day, $F$ by at most $2$ days at $\$100$ per day, and $E$ by at most $1$ day at $\$60$ per day. Starting from the original durations, find the greatest project saving and its least cost.
